# IMPLEMENTATION OF PROTECTION FOR WOMEN AND CHILDREN

REGENT OF TABALONG

PROVINCE OF SOUTH KALIMANTAN

# REGIONAL REGULATION OF TABALONG REGENCY

NUMBER 04 OF 2017

CONCERNING

IMPLEMENTATION OF PROTECTION FOR WOMEN AND CHILDREN

BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD

REGENT OF TABALONG,

Considering:

a. that every citizen has the right to be free from torture or treatment that degrades human dignity and has the right to obtain security and freedom from all forms of violence;
b. that all forms of violence against women and children constitute violations of human rights so that their dignity must be protected and their right to life guaranteed in accordance with their nature without discrimination;
c. that the Regional Government is obligated to implement protection for women and children;
d. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b and letter c, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning the Implementation of Protection for Women and Children;

1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;
2. Law Number 8 of 1965 concerning the Establishment of Second Level Region of Tanah Laut, Second Level Region of Tapin and Second Level Region of Tabalong (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1965 Number 51, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 2756);
3. Law Number 4 of 1979 concerning Child Welfare (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1979 Number 32, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3143);
4. Law Number 8 of 1981 concerning Criminal Procedure Law (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1981 Number 76, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3209);
5. Law Number 39 of 1999 concerning Human Rights (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1999 Number 165, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3886);
6. Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2002 Number 109, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4235), as amended by Law Number 35 of 2014 concerning Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 297, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5606);
7. Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2004 Number 95, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4419);
8. Law Number 13 of 2006 concerning Protection of Witnesses and Victims (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2006 Number 64, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4635);
9. Law Number 21 of 2007 concerning the Eradication of the Criminal Act of Trafficking in Persons (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2007 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4720);
10. Law Number 10 of 2012 concerning the Optional Protocol to the Convention on the Rights of the Child on the Sale of Children, Child Prostitution, and Child Pornography (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2012 Number 149, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5330);
11. Law Number 11 of 2012 concerning the Juvenile Criminal Justice System (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2012 Number 153, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5332);
12. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587), as amended several times, most recently by Law Number 9 of 2015 concerning the Second Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2015 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5679);
13. Government Regulation Number 27 of 1983 concerning the Implementation of the Criminal Procedure Code (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1983 Number 36, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3258);
14. Government Regulation Number 40 of 2011 concerning Guidance, Assistance, and Recovery for Children Who Are Victims or Perpetrators of Pornography (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2007 Number 86, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5237);
15. Presidential Regulation Number 18 of 2014 concerning Protection and Empowerment of Women and Children in Social Conflict (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 44);
16. Regulation of the Minister of Home Affairs Number 15 of 2008 concerning General Guidelines for the Implementation of Gender Mainstreaming in the Regions, as amended by Regulation of the Minister of Home Affairs Number 67 of 2011 concerning Amendment to Regulation of the Minister of Home Affairs Number 15 of 2008 concerning General Guidelines for the Implementation of Gender Mainstreaming in the Regions (State News of the Republic of Indonesia of 2011 Number 927);
17. Regional Regulation of Tabalong Regency Number 05 of 2016 concerning the Establishment and Composition of Regional Apparatus (Regional Gazette of Tabalong Regency of 2016 Number 05, Supplement to the Regional Gazette of Tabalong Regency Number 02);

With Mutual Approval

REGIONAL HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES OF TABALONG REGENCY

and

REGENT OF TABALONG

DECIDES:

To Establish:

REGIONAL REGULATION CONCERNING THE IMPLEMENTATION OF PROTECTION FOR WOMEN AND CHILDREN.

# CHAPTER I

## GENERAL PROVISIONS

Article 1 In this Regional Regulation, what is meant by:
1. Region is Tabalong Regency.
2. Regional Government is the regional head as an element of the Regional Government administration who leads the implementation of government affairs that are the authority of the autonomous region.
3. Regional Head hereinafter referred to as Regent is the Regent of Tabalong.
4. Regional Apparatus Organization hereinafter abbreviated as OPD is an auxiliary element of the Regent and DPRD in the administration of Government Affairs that are the authority of the Region.
5. Agency is the Agency for Women's Empowerment, Child Protection, Population Control and Family Planning of Tabalong Regency.
6. Head of Agency is the Head of the Agency for Women's Empowerment, Child Protection, Population Control and Family Planning of Tabalong Regency.
7. Gender is a concept that refers to the differentiation of roles, functions and responsibilities of men and women that occur as a result of and can be changed by the social and cultural conditions of society.
8. Gender-based violence is any deviant act caused by an imbalance of power in the relationship between women and men that results in misery or suffering of women and children whether physically, sexually and/or psychologically including threats of certain actions, coercion or deprivation of freedom arbitrarily that occurs in the private/domestic sphere and in the public sphere.
9. Protection is all efforts aimed at providing a sense of security to women and children carried out by family, advocates, social institutions, police, prosecutors, courts, or other parties either temporarily or based on court determination.
10. Woman is an adult human being of female sex and a person recognized by law as a woman.
11. Child is a person who has not reached 18 years of age including the fetus in the womb.
12. Victim is a woman and child who experiences violence and/or suffering as a result of violence and/or threat of violence.
13. Integrated Service Center for Women and Children Empowerment hereinafter referred to as P2TP2A is an Integrated Activity Center that provides services for women and children victims of violence in Tabalong Regency free of charge including information services, psychological, legal and religious consultation, assistance and advocacy as well as health services and safe houses by referral.

